der of established European and east Asian arthouse: he takes us from the cine-prehistory of photographer <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/2010/sep/04/eadweard-muybridge-exhibition-rebecca-solnit">Eadweard Muybridge</a> to Fritz Langâ€™s Metropolis, DW Griffithâ€™s Birth of a Nation with its sinister Ku Klux Klan hero-worship, Chaplin, Stroheim, Hitchcock, Capra, Renoir, Bogart, Marilyn Monroe in The Seven-Year Itch, Monroe Stahr in The Last Tycoon, Scorseseâ€™s GoodFellas, David Lynchâ€™s Mulholland Drive (â€œIs it drive or dream?â€), Kirk&nbsp;Douglas and his alleged rape of Natalie Wood, Barbara Lodenâ€™s Wanda, Sean Bakerâ€™s Anora, Tracey Eminâ€™s Why I Never Became a Dancer and much more. He subtitles his book a â€œrevisionistâ€ history.</p> <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/books/2026/jul/20/a-sudden-flicker-of-light-by-david-thomson-review-a-brilliantly-eccentric-history-of-the-movies">Continue reading...</a>ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;e8BhKpDRhmCNXevdhSQqTMxTo5pVBAqTGK8fgv62QtMƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxcA Sudden Flicker of Light by David Thomson review â€“ a brilliantly eccentric history of the moviesƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;LyVzyy9LV9359VmFPLiEjU6J-TTxwcvAJotsvMGMDLIƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkoSyndicationItemƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;tP8syn6nCZdoIJiajSI14kIYsvsYIh4RIrBsiNvkMO0ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxhttps://www.theguardian.com/books/2026/jul/20/a-sudden-flicker-of-light-by-david-thomson-review-a-brilliantly-eccentric-history-of-the-moviesƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;fW5Gu8YgFEcLTQ82BbqXuVh3wvhW6KvAYgKPOxcQbvkƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx_a-